INT. ZOO REPTILE HOUSE - OFFICE - DAY

Cluttered desk. A taxidermy iguana on a filing cabinet. An intercom box on the wall.

ELEANOR "NELLIE" BRIGHTWATER (40s, khaki vest, perpetually frazzled) runs a hand through her hair. Across from her, new hire PERCIVAL ADEWALE-STONE (20s, brand-new uniform, a clipboard clutched to his chest) sits rigidly.

NELLIE
So. Your first day.

PERCIVAL
Yes. I'm very excited.

NELLIE
Don't be.

INTERCOM (V.O.)
Nellie, it's the snake house. Mamba's out.

Nellie shuts her eyes. Percival stares at the intercom.

PERCIVAL
Out of what?

NELLIE
Out of everything.

She leaps to her feet and knocks the desk; papers go flying. Percival ducks, and they tangle in the doorway, jostling, pushing, shoving each other out into the corridor.

INTERCOM (V.O.) (CONT'D)
Also the python. And the gift shop.

PERCIVAL
The gift shop?

NELLIE
Nobody panic.

PERCIVAL
Everyone's panicking.

NELLIE
Percival, you're holding the clipboard upside down.

PERCIVAL
That's my panic.

They scatter down the hall in two directions, shouting.
